IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`
IMPORT `g3-art9-restricted-section`
IMPORT `g3-art10-public-access`
IMPORT `g5-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-art27-28-required-steps`
IMPORT `int-readings`
IMPORT `int-nouns`
IMPORT `int-commencement`
IMPORT `int-vintage`
IMPORT `int-wiring`

-- int-h-register.l4: headline (b) of the integration layer: is this entity a registered charity on this day, and what does the register hold about it?
-- "Registered charity" is Article 1's definition (group G1): an entity entered for the time being in the general or the restricted section, and NOT the historic section (trap T7). Where the entity stands is the register's
-- own record, which group G3 reads from the dated entries (Article 8(2)); what the register must hold about it is Article 8(3) (registered charity), 8(5) (formerly registered, historic section) and 9(1) (the public
-- elements of the restricted section), each read by group G3 from facts produced by the groups that decide them: the charity test only by virtue of an Order (G2, IP10), the required steps notices (G8, IP19),
-- the Order under Article 13(9)(c) (G5, IP29) and the organized religious charity (G8, IP20).
-- It rests on Articles 1, 2, 5, 8, 9, 10 and refuses for a day before Part 4 (1 May 2018) and for a day on which the text changed and the two texts answer differently.

§ `Integration layer -- headline (b): is the entity a registered charity, and what does the register hold?`

-- The case: a body, what the register records about it, and the facts the Articles on the register read.
DECLARE `Register entry in the case` HAS
    body IS A `Body in the case` @desc The entity and its people; its standing is the register's record (an input) and is checked against the dated entries
    `charity test facts` IS A `Facts for the charity test in the case` @desc The facts the charity test reads (Article 5), which Article 8(3)(i) needs only to say whether the entity meets it by virtue of an Order
    placements IS A LIST OF `Placement of an entity in a section of the register` @desc Every entry of the entity in a section of the register, with its date; empty if it has never been entered (Article 8(2))
    `registration number` IS A STRING @desc The number allocated under Article 12(2)(b)
    `registered name` IS A STRING @desc The registered name entered under Article 12(2)(a)
    `alternative registered names` IS A LIST OF STRING @desc Further names entered under Article 12(5)
    `date registered` IS A DATE @desc The date on which the charity was registered (Article 8(3)(g))
    `date deregistered` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING while the entity is registered; the effective date of deregistration otherwise
    `registered charitable purposes` IS A LIST OF STRING @desc The purposes in the statement approved under Article 8(3)(e)
    `registered public benefit statement` IS A STRING @desc The statement approved under Article 8(3)(f)
    `Order under Article 28` IS AN `Order under Article 28 as it applies to a charity` @desc The Order categorizing organized religious charities, as it applies to this charity, and the Commissioner's grant or withdrawal of the status (Article 28)
    `Order under Article 13(9)` IS A MAYBE `Order under Article 13(9)` @desc The Order under Article 13(9); NOTHING if none
    `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS A LIST OF `Order under Article 13(10)` @desc The Orders under Article 13(10) that relieve small charities
    `facts for the items of Article 8(3)` IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` @desc Other premises, the principal address entered, previous registered names and the information an Order prescribes (Article 8(3))
    `facts for the items of Article 8(5)` IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)` @desc The placements before deregistration, previous names and the matters an Order prescribes (Article 8(5))
    `facts for the public elements` IS A `Facts for the public elements (Article 9(1))` @desc Whether a summary of reasons has been produced, and whether an Order prescribes another public element (Article 9(1))
    `facts for the principal address` IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` @desc The registered office, the main premises and the governors' addresses in Jersey (Article 8(4))
    `notices served` IS A LIST OF `Notice served in the case` @desc The required steps notices served on the charity or its governors (Article 27)

DECLARE `Answer on the register` HAS
    entity IS AN Entity @desc The entity as Article 2 leaves it (IP5), with the standing the register records
    `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP6, group G1: Article 1: entered in the general or the restricted section (not the historic section)
    `section the entity is entered in` IS A MAYBE `Section of the register` @desc Group G3: Article 8(2): the section of the latest entry that has taken effect by the day; NOTHING if never entered
    `the recorded standing agrees with the entries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the standing the register records (an input) is the standing the dated entries give on the day (the integrator's check of IP6 and IP7)
    `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP10, group G2: Article 5(3)
    `the entity is an organized religious charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP20, group G8: Article 28
    `the entries the Commissioner must enter` IS A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(3)` @desc Group G3: Article 8(3), for a registered charity; empty otherwise
    `the entries the Commissioner must enter in the historic section` IS A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(5)` @desc Group G3: Article 8(5), for a formerly registered charity; empty otherwise
    `the public elements of the restricted section` IS A LIST OF `Element of the restricted section (Article 9(1))` @desc Group G3: Article 9(1), for a charity in the restricted section; empty otherwise
    `the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` IS A LIST OF STRING @desc Group G3: Article 8(4)
    `the entity has a principal address in Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP17, group G3: Article 8(4)

-- The register's section named by the standing.
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register` @desc Where the register records the entity
GIVETH A MAYBE `Section of the register`
`Int the section that a standing names` standing MEANS
    CONSIDER standing
      WHEN `not on the register` THEN NOTHING
      WHEN `an applicant for registration` THEN NOTHING
      WHEN `entered in the general section` THEN JUST `the general section`
      WHEN `entered in the restricted section` THEN JUST `the restricted section`
      WHEN `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` THEN JUST `the historic section`

-- IP7: the register's record of the entity. Group G3 gives the entries; the organized-religious flag is IP20 (group G8); the date deregistered is set by group G6 in the Articles that deregister.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      entity IS AN Entity @desc The entity (IP5)
      case IS A `Register entry in the case` @desc The case
GIVETH A `Registered charity`
`Int IP7 the registered charity` readings entity case MEANS
    `Registered charity` WITH
        entity IS entity
        `registration number` IS case's `registration number`
        `registered name` IS case's `registered name`
        `alternative registered names` IS case's `alternative registered names`
        `date registered` IS case's `date registered`
        `date deregistered` IS case's `date deregistered`
        `registered charitable purposes` IS case's `registered charitable purposes`
        `registered public benefit statement` IS case's `registered public benefit statement`
        `is an organized religious charity` IS `Art 28 the entity is an organized religious charity` (`Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` entity) (case's `Order under Article 28`)

-- The answer under ONE text of the Law.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law
      case IS A `Register entry in the case` @desc The case
GIVETH AN `Answer on the register`
`Int (b) the answer on the register under the text` readings day vintage case MEANS
    `Answer on the register` WITH
        entity IS entity
        `the entity is a registered charity` IS `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` entity
        `section the entity is entered in` IS section
        `the recorded standing agrees with the entries` IS `Int the section that a standing names` ((case's body)'s standing) EQUALS section
        `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order` IS only
        `the entity is an organized religious charity` IS registeredCharity's `is an organized religious charity`
        `the entries the Commissioner must enter` IS
            IF `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` entity
            THEN `Art 8(3) the entries required for the registered charity` (readings's `reading of Articles 8 to 10`) registeredCharity only notices (`Int IP29 an Order under Article 13(9)(c) applies` readings (case's `Order under Article 13(9)`) (case's `relief Orders under Article 13(10)`)) (case's `facts for the items of Article 8(3)`)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the entries the Commissioner must enter in the historic section` IS
            IF section EQUALS JUST `the historic section`
            THEN `Art 8(5) the entries required in the historic section` (readings's `reading of Articles 8 to 10`) registeredCharity (case's `facts for the items of Article 8(5)`)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the public elements of the restricted section` IS
            IF section EQUALS JUST `the restricted section`
            THEN `Art 9(1) the public elements of the restricted section` (readings's `reading of Articles 8 to 10`) registeredCharity notices (case's `facts for the public elements`)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` IS `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` (readings's `reading of Articles 8 to 10`) entity (case's `facts for the principal address`)
        `the entity has a principal address in Jersey` IS `Int IP17 the entity has a principal address in Jersey` readings entity (case's `facts for the principal address`)
    WHERE
        notices MEANS `Int IP19 the required steps notices served` readings (case's `notices served`)
        entity MEANS `Int IP5 the entity` readings vintage notices day (case's body)
        section MEANS `Art 8(2) the section in which the entity is entered on` (readings's `reading of Articles 8 to 10`) (case's placements) day
        only MEANS `Int IP10 the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order` readings vintage entity ((case's body)'s purposes) (case's `charity test facts`)
        registeredCharity MEANS `Int IP7 the registered charity` readings entity case

`Int (b) the units the question rests on` MEANS
    LIST `Int Article` 1, `Int Article` 2, `Int Article` 5, `Int Article` 8, `Int Article` 9, `Int Article` 10

@export Is this entity a registered charity on a given day, and what does the register hold about it: whether it is entered in the general or the restricted section (Article 1; the historic section does not count), the section its dated entries put it in (Article 8(2)), and the entries the Commissioner must make (Article 8(3) for a registered charity, Article 8(5) for a formerly registered one, Article 9(1) for the public elements of the restricted section). Refuses for a day before Part 4 of the Law was in force (1 May 2018), and for a day on which the text of the Law changed and the two texts answer differently
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups (the favoured readings are `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`)
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked, for example 2026-10-02 (ISO 8601)
      case IS A `Register entry in the case` @desc The entity, what the register records about it, and the facts the Articles on the register read
GIVETH AN `Answer on the register`
`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` readings day case MEANS
    `Int the answer if every unit is in force` `Int (b) the units the question rests on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        (`Int the answer under every text of the Law in force on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
            (GIVEN vintage YIELD `Int (b) the answer on the register under the text` readings day vintage case))
